            <ArticleTitle>Catalytic Enantioselective Double Carbopalladation/C-H Functionalization with Statistical Amplification of Product Enantiopurity: A Convertible Linker Approach.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>14192-14196</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1002/anie.201709133</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Combining a catalytic enantioselective reaction with dimerization in a single operation is an efficient way to upgrade the enantiomeric excesses (ee) of the product. Palladium-catalyzed reaction of N-(2-iodophenyl)-N-methyl methacrylamide derivatives with oxadiazole afforded, by a double enantioselective carbopalladation/intermolecular heteroarene C-H alkylation sequence, homodimers in good yields with excellent ee values. The dimer was subsequently elaborated to the monomer in which the linker (oxadiazole) was incorporated into the target product.</AbstractText>
